BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afrikan Drumming Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T150000
UID:6a05f1605cfd98bf7cee6ad9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Storyteller and professional percussionist\, Kwanza Msingwana\
 , performs folktales and traditional stories from Afrika and around the wo
 rld\, and/or performs traditional Afrikan drumming. The program is rooted 
 in interactive storytelling of stories\, folktales and drumming from Afrik
 a as well as the Caribbean\, the Americas\, and around the world.\nThis pr
 ogram is intended for all children and their families.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a05f1605cfd98bf7cee6ad9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
