BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Moana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T120000
UID:6a01e82cf6bd012f006725a8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a movie on the big screen! Bring a friend\, and a 
 snack!\nMoana (2016)\n1h47min Rated: G\nMoana\nis an exciting animated mus
 ical about a brave Polynesian teenager named Moana who sails across the oc
 ean to save her island home. Along with the shape-shifting demigod Maui\, 
 she faces sea monsters\, learns to navigate\, and restores a magical heart
  to a goddess\, discovering her true strength.\n*This program is suitable 
 for all ages\; younger children must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.
  Drop in!*
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a01e82cf6bd012f006725a8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
