BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Paddling Puppeteer - Plugging into Nature
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T144500
UID:69fba79ae8af4a2f0070abf8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Paddling Puppeteers (Glen Caradus) presents a musical pupp
 et show promoting nearby nature connection\, urban stewardship and wellnes
 s. It's a show full of songs and colourful puppets!\nEdward loves his vide
 o games and indoor time. One day he goes outside and discovers the natural
  world. He meets a chickadee\, butterfly and frog who guide Edward on a pa
 th of outdoor fun and wellness. At the end of the show\, Edward helps to "
 plant up" the "neighbourwood." Edward still loves his screen time\, but he
  also loves getting outside.\nSpace is limited. Tickets will be given out 
 30 minutes prior from the main desk at Swansea Memorial branch.\nWith than
 ks to the Swansea Town Hall for funding this special event and providing t
 he room.
LOCATION:Swansea Memorial\, Rousseau Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fba79ae8af4a2f0070abf8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
