BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scientists in School: Science Meets Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T150000
UID:69c2ee2a274a65e67a909676@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover what happens when science meets art! Explore percepti
 on as you use shadows\, colour\, motion\, and light to create art from sci
 ence. You’ll make a puppet\, a spinning top and a kaleidoscope\, as well
  as design your own galaxy. “The greatest scientists are always artists 
 as well!” (Albert Einstein) Please note: this program is suitable for ch
 ildren 4 years old and above with adult accompaniment. This program allows
  up to 25 children with their parents and guardians.\nWhen registering\, p
 lease only include children in the total number of people attending.\nScie
 ntists in School is a leading national science\, technology\, engineering 
 and math (STEM) education charity that is dedicated to providing programs 
 for children and youth across Canada.  Programs are designed to build conf
 idence in STEM and develop critical thinking skills. The mission of Scient
 ists in School is to ignite scientific curiosity in children so that they 
 question intelligently\; learn through discovery\; connect scientific know
 ledge to their world\; are excited about science\, technology\, engineerin
 g and math\; and have their interest in careers in those fields piqued.​
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON 
 M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c2ee2a274a65e67a909676
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
