DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T150000
UID:69f10da5b6c4ac1fedcf7565@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pawsitively Pets is a hands-on animal education program that o
 ffers positive animal interactions for children and adults of all ages. Jo
 in us and enjoy interacting with a variety of animals\, while learning abo
 ut the responsibilities of pet ownership!\nChildren attending this event m
 ust be accompanied by an adult. When registering\, please indicate how man
 y\nchildren\nare attending. This program can accommodate up to 25 children
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
